## Consequences

1. Paper 2 is not a line-by-line merger of A001 and A002.
2. A002 controls typed restricted conservation, observation, sampled/hybrid/information, and projectability results.
3. A001 contributes general viability/recovery, unique obstructions, CES, bounded composition, and selected finite-horizon/intergenerational results after correction.
4. Resource-domain, dynamical, institutional, and empirical theorem families move to the papers whose questions require them.
5. Elementary monotonicity and definition-level results are stated once and proved once.

## Remaining gate

Exact proof verification still controls every retained row. This source-selection decision reduces duplication but does not certify the selected proofs.